e <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is the length of the side opposite the 30<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment--> angle. Segment <span class=\"italic\">PQ</span> is opposite the 30<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment--> angle. Therefore, 2(<span class=\"italic\">PQ</span>)<span class=\"italic\"></span> = 8 and <span class=\"italic\">PQ </span>= 4.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":2,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959636,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"13d9a1c3","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959636,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"09170-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"ca8aad09-e2a4-410a-8c8a-6a1768acefd1","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"09170-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle P Q R, where side P R is horizontal, and point Q is directly above point P. Angle P is a right angle. Angle R is labeled 30 degrees and side Q R is labeled 8.\" width=\"99\" height=\"63\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the right triangle shown above, what is the length of&nbsp;<span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line P Q\"></span></span>&nbsp;?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p class=\"tcp-fd3ea050-58f4-4b16-a81d-baba01ecbcd1\">The correct answer is 4. Triangle <span class=\"italic\">PQR </span>has given angle measures of 30<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment--> and 90<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment-->, so the third angle must be 60&deg; because the measures of the angles of a triangle sum to 180<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment-->. For any special right triangle with angles measuring 30&deg;, 60&deg;, and 90&deg;, the length of the hypotenuse (the side opposite the right angle) is 2<span class=\"italic\">x</span>, where <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is the length of the side opposite the 30<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment--> angle. Segment <span class=\"italic\">PQ</span> is opposite the 30<!--StartFragment-->&deg;<!--EndFragment--> angle. Therefore, 2(<span class=\"italic\">PQ</span>)<span class=\"italic\"></span> = 8 and <span class=\"italic\">PQ </span>= 4.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959636,"updateDate":1691007959636,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959636, 1691007959636),
