     <use x=\"415.136719\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-114\"></use>\n     <use x=\"452.246094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use>\n     <use x=\"494.238281\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use>\n     <use x=\"516.601562\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-110\"></use>\n     <use x=\"569.628906\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-111\"></use>\n     <use x=\"619.433594\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-116\"></use>\n     <use x=\"650.097656\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use>\n     <use x=\"672.460938\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-100\"></use>\n     <use x=\"720.996094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-114\"></use>\n     <use x=\"758.105469\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-97\"></use>\n     <use x=\"799.414062\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-119\"></use>\n     <use x=\"871.09375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-110\"></use>\n     <use x=\"924.121094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use>\n     <use x=\"946.484375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-116\"></use>\n     <use x=\"977.148438\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-111\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1026.953125\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1049.316406\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-115\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1084.375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-99\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1123.925781\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-97\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1165.234375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-108\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1189.746094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1231.738281\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-46\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n</g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(23, 18) scale(1 1) \">\n      <polygon points=\"192.491 0.945 192.491 146.149 0.945 146.149 192.491 0.945\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon>\n      <rect x=\"181.151\" y=\"134.809\" width=\"11.34\" height=\"11.34\" stroke-width=\"0.945\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"></rect>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for right triangle\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>One angle is a right angle.</li><li>The measure of the other 2 angles are as follows:<br><ul><li>45°</li><li>45°</li></ul></li><li>The lengths of the 2 sides adjacent to the right angle are as follows:<br><ul><li>x</li><li>24</li></ul></li><li>Note: Figure not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the triangle shown, what is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["d841bf0c-037c-4a9c-9ed2-4cd4cad575f7"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"d841bf0c-037c-4a9c-9ed2-4cd4cad575f7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4c27d95c-2c77-4da9-a799-6a8b61f41175","content":"<p><math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4b9e8a04-9f1f-4bf9-b915-14a795e95069","content":"<p><math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"acbc3864-15a2-47f4-acc0-9aacdd21a0a9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"69\"><mn>69</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. Since the two acute angles have the same measure and the third angle is a right angle, the triangle shown is an isosceles right triangle. In an isosceles right triangle, the two legs have the same length. The figure shows that the length of one leg of the triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn></math> and the length of the other leg of the triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>. It follows that the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of one of the angles shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"7e480092-1ead-484d-8b6f-5c6417fa9d9f","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1755117017720,"updateDate":1755117017720}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017720, 1755117017720),
    ($SATQ$14e7c1f4$SATQ$, $SATQ$889dae43-01c0-449b-abd7-1a385a85c6a7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">For two acute angles,&nbsp;<math alttext="angle upper Q"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>Q</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math>. The measures, in degrees, of&nbsp;<math alttext="angle upper Q"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are <math alttext="x plus 61"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>61</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="4 x plus 4"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>4</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, respectively. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce9d7c1a-da11-49a1-9bf0-53d57615d954","content":"<p><math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90ce9205-5941-4e10-9b17-4c354281d547","content":"<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cbdab634-8172-4af8-a49b-20e0c1d30093","content":"<p><math alttext=\"29\"><mn>29</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that for two acute angles,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper Q"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. For two acute angles, if the sine of one angle is equal to the cosine of the other angle, the angles are complementary. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper Q"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are complementary. That is, the sum of the measures of the angles is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="90"><mn>90</mn></math> degrees. It's given that the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper Q"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 61"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn></math> degrees and the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 x plus 4"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> degrees. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x plus 61 right parenthesis plus left parenthesis 4 x plus 4 right parenthesis equals 90"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. By combining like terms, this equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x plus 65 equals 90"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="65"><mn>65</mn></math> from each side of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 x equals 25"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 5"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. This would be the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This would be the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals minus cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and if <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="angle upper R"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> were obtuse rather than acute.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"14e7c1f4","external_id":"889dae43-01c0-449b-abd7-1a385a85c6a7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e9dbf29b-e790-40bc-b026-fae5bd340a22","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For two acute angles,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>Q</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math>. The measures, in degrees, of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are <math alttext=\"x plus 61\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>61</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"4 x plus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, respectively. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce9d7c1a-da11-49a1-9bf0-53d57615d954","content":"<p><math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90ce9205-5941-4e10-9b17-4c354281d547","content":"<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cbdab634-8172-4af8-a49b-20e0c1d30093","content":"<p><math alttext=\"29\"><mn>29</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that for two acute angles,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. For two acute angles, if the sine of one angle is equal to the cosine of the other angle, the angles are complementary. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are complementary. That is, the sum of the measures of the angles is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn></math> degrees. It's given that the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus 61\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn></math> degrees and the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x plus 4\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> degrees. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 61 right parenthesis plus left parenthesis 4 x plus 4 right parenthesis equals 90\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. By combining like terms, this equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x plus 65 equals 90\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"65\"><mn>65</mn></math> from each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 25\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 5\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This would be the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This would be the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals minus cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> were obtuse rather than acute.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017720,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"14e7c1f4","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1755117017720,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"889dae43-01c0-449b-abd7-1a385a85c6a7","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"e9dbf29b-e790-40bc-b026-fae5bd340a22","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For two acute angles,&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>Q</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math>. The measures, in degrees, of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are <math alttext=\"x plus 61\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>61</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"4 x plus 4\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, respectively. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"dfb682ad-36d0-4bb7-bd3a-1322345db8ed","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce9d7c1a-da11-49a1-9bf0-53d57615d954","content":"<p><math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90ce9205-5941-4e10-9b17-4c354281d547","content":"<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cbdab634-8172-4af8-a49b-20e0c1d30093","content":"<p><math alttext=\"29\"><mn>29</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that for two acute angles,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. For two acute angles, if the sine of one angle is equal to the cosine of the other angle, the angles are complementary. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are complementary. That is, the sum of the measures of the angles is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn></math> degrees. It's given that the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper Q\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus 61\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn></math> degrees and the measure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 x plus 4\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> degrees. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 61 right parenthesis plus left parenthesis 4 x plus 4 right parenthesis equals 90\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. By combining like terms, this equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x plus 65 equals 90\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"65\"><mn>65</mn></math> from each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 x equals 25\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 5\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This would be the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This would be the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals minus cosine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine left parenthesis upper Q right parenthesis equals sine left parenthesis upper R right parenthesis\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"angle upper R\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> were obtuse rather than acute.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"889dae43-01c0-449b-abd7-1a385a85c6a7","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1755117017720,"updateDate":1755117017720}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017720, 1755117017720),
    ($SATQ$151eda3c$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$06614-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">A manufacturing company produces two sizes of cylindrical containers that each have a height of 50 centimeters. The radius of container A is 16 centimeters, and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of container B?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_000_3a923f8f.png\" alt=\"16,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_001_077cf80f.png\" alt=\"20,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_002_461394e7.png\" alt=\"25,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_003_2d71c755.png\" alt=\"31,250 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. If the radius of container A is 16 centimeters and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A, then the radius of container B is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_004_cdffae2a.png" alt="16 plus, 0 point 2 5 times 16, equals 20"></span> centimeters. The volume of a cylinder is <span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_005_c51c04dc.png" alt="pi, times r squared, times h"></span></span>, where <span class="italic">r</span> is the radius of the cylinder and <span class="italic">h</span> is its height. Substituting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_006_c322f014.png" alt="r equals 20"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_007_48bf376c.png" alt="h equals 50"></span> into <span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_008_c51c04dc.png" alt="pi, times r squared, times h"></span></span> yields that the volume of cylinder B is <span class="italic"><span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_009_20e601f3.png" alt="pi times open parenthesis, 20, close parenthesis, squared, times 50, equals 20,000 pi"></span></span></span> cubic centimeters.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by the radius of cylinder A rather than squaring the radius of cylinder B. Choice C is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by 25 rather than squaring it. Choice D is incorrect and may result from taking the radius of cylinder B to be 25 centimeters rather than 20 centimeters.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"151eda3c","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"06614-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A manufacturing company produces two sizes of cylindrical containers that each have a height of 50 centimeters. The radius of container A is 16 centimeters, and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of container B?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_000_3a923f8f.png\" alt=\"16,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_001_077cf80f.png\" alt=\"20,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_002_461394e7.png\" alt=\"25,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_003_2d71c755.png\" alt=\"31,250 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. If the radius of container A is 16 centimeters and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A, then the radius of container B is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_004_cdffae2a.png\" alt=\"16 plus, 0 point 2 5 times 16, equals 20\"></span> centimeters. The volume of a cylinder is <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_005_c51c04dc.png\" alt=\"pi, times r squared, times h\"></span></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">r</span> is the radius of the cylinder and <span class=\"italic\">h</span> is its height. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_006_c322f014.png\" alt=\"r equals 20\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_007_48bf376c.png\" alt=\"h equals 50\"></span> into <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_008_c51c04dc.png\" alt=\"pi, times r squared, times h\"></span></span> yields that the volume of cylinder B is <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/151eda3c/img_009_20e601f3.png\" alt=\"pi times open parenthesis, 20, close parenthesis, squared, times 50, equals 20,000 pi\"></span></span></span> cubic centimeters.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by the radius of cylinder A rather than squaring the radius of cylinder B. Choice C is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by 25 rather than squaring it. Choice D is incorrect and may result from taking the radius of cylinder B to be 25 centimeters rather than 20 centimeters.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":10,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959630,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"151eda3c","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1691007959630,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"06614-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"35b5fdf9-0760-485d-9e7a-65162686bb38","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"06614-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A manufacturing company produces two sizes of cylindrical containers that each have a height of 50 centimeters. The radius of container A is 16 centimeters, and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of container B?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"16,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"20,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"25,000 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"31,250 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. If the radius of container A is 16 centimeters and the radius of container B is 25% longer than the radius of container A, then the radius of container B is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"16 plus, 0 point 2 5 times 16, equals 20\"></span> centimeters. The volume of a cylinder is <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi, times r squared, times h\"></span></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">r</span> is the radius of the cylinder and <span class=\"italic\">h</span> is its height. Substituting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"r equals 20\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"h equals 50\"></span> into <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi, times r squared, times h\"></span></span> yields that the volume of cylinder B is <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi times open parenthesis, 20, close parenthesis, squared, times 50, equals 20,000 pi\"></span></span></span> cubic centimeters.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by the radius of cylinder A rather than squaring the radius of cylinder B. Choice C is incorrect and may result from multiplying the radius of cylinder B by 25 rather than squaring it. Choice D is incorrect and may result from taking the radius of cylinder B to be 25 centimeters rather than 20 centimeters.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959630,"updateDate":1691007959630}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959630, 1691007959630),
    ($SATQ$165c30c4$SATQ$, $SATQ$7ce3a2e8-bebb-4040-84e7-3f30170327e3$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$82b62cde-74a1-42c3-a1ec-41c10ea7600f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A rectangle has a length of <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
