</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"167aff9e","external_id":"ca49552d-a377-4804-b20d-7b730e15bb99","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"37536a88-8579-4e8b-a034-ea4924de3e90","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Right rectangular prism X is similar to right rectangular prism Y. The surface area of right rectangular prism X is <math alttext=\"58 square centimeters left parenthesis cm squared right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>58</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, and the surface area of right rectangular prism Y is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"1,450 cm squared\"><mrow><mn>1,450</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;The volume of right rectangular prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,250 cubic centimeters left parenthesis cm cubed right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>1,250</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cubic</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mfenced></math>. What is the sum of the volumes, <math alttext=\"in cm cubed\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, of right rectangular prism X and right rectangular prism Y?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["1260"],"correct_answer":["1260"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"1,260\"><mn>1,260</mn>\n</math>. Since it's given that prisms X and Y are similar, all the linear measurements of prism Y are <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> times the respective linear measurements of prism X, where <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant. Therefore, the surface area of prism Y is <math alttext=\"k squared\"><msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> times the surface area of prism X and the volume of prism Y is <math alttext=\"k cubed\"><msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> times the volume of prism X. It's given that the surface area of prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,450 c m squared\"><mn>1,450</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, and the surface area of prism X is <math alttext=\"58 c m squared\"><mn>58</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which implies that <math alttext=\"1,450 equals 58 k squared\"><mrow>\n<mn>1,450</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>58</mn>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"58\"><mn>58</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,450 Over 58 EndFraction equals k squared\"><mfrac><mn>1,450</mn><mn>58</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"k squared equals 25\"><mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>25</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant, <math alttext=\"k equals 5\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It's given that the volume of prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,250 c m cubed\"><mn>1,250</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the volume of prism X is equal to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,250 Over k cubed EndFraction c m cubed\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>1,250</mn>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</msup>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,250 Over 5 cubed EndFraction c m cubed\"><mfrac><mn>1,250</mn><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"10 c m cubed\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the sum of the volumes, in <math alttext=\"c m cubed\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, of the two prisms is <math alttext=\"1,250 plus 10\"><mn>1,250</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"1,260\"><mn>1,260</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554986,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"167aff9e","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1743430554986,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"ca49552d-a377-4804-b20d-7b730e15bb99","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"37536a88-8579-4e8b-a034-ea4924de3e90","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Right rectangular prism X is similar to right rectangular prism Y. The surface area of right rectangular prism X is <math alttext=\"58 square centimeters left parenthesis cm squared right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>58</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, and the surface area of right rectangular prism Y is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"1,450 cm squared\"><mrow><mn>1,450</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;The volume of right rectangular prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,250 cubic centimeters left parenthesis cm cubed right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>1,250</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cubic</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></mfenced></math>. What is the sum of the volumes, <math alttext=\"in cm cubed\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, of right rectangular prism X and right rectangular prism Y?</p>","keys":["1260"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"1,260\"><mn>1,260</mn>\n</math>. Since it's given that prisms X and Y are similar, all the linear measurements of prism Y are <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> times the respective linear measurements of prism X, where <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant. Therefore, the surface area of prism Y is <math alttext=\"k squared\"><msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> times the surface area of prism X and the volume of prism Y is <math alttext=\"k cubed\"><msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> times the volume of prism X. It's given that the surface area of prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,450 c m squared\"><mn>1,450</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, and the surface area of prism X is <math alttext=\"58 c m squared\"><mn>58</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which implies that <math alttext=\"1,450 equals 58 k squared\"><mrow>\n<mn>1,450</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>58</mn>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"58\"><mn>58</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,450 Over 58 EndFraction equals k squared\"><mfrac><mn>1,450</mn><mn>58</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"k squared equals 25\"><mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>25</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant, <math alttext=\"k equals 5\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It's given that the volume of prism Y is <math alttext=\"1,250 c m cubed\"><mn>1,250</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the volume of prism X is equal to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,250 Over k cubed EndFraction c m cubed\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>1,250</mn>\n<msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</msup>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1,250 Over 5 cubed EndFraction c m cubed\"><mfrac><mn>1,250</mn><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"10 c m cubed\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the sum of the volumes, in <math alttext=\"c m cubed\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, of the two prisms is <math alttext=\"1,250 plus 10\"><mn>1,250</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"1,260\"><mn>1,260</mn>\n</math>.</p>","externalid":"ca49552d-a377-4804-b20d-7b730e15bb99","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["1260"]},"createDate":1743430554986,"updateDate":1743430554986}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554986, 1743430554986),
