<p style="text-align: left;">Circle A shown is defined by the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="x squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals 7"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. Circle B (not shown) has the same radius but is translated <math alttext="96"><mn>96</mn>
</math> units to the right. If the equation of circle B is <math alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals a"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, where <math alttext="h"><mi>h</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> are constants, what is the value of <math alttext="4 a"><mrow>
	<mn>4</mn>
	<mi>a</mi>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["28"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["28"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math>. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus t right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus s right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis t comma s right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that circle A is defined by the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals 7"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 0 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 6 right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis StartRoot 7 EndRoot right parenthesis squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r equals StartRoot 7 EndRoot"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> and the radius of circle A is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 7 EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that circle B has the same radius as circle A. If the equation of circle B is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals a"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, then <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals r squared"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 7 EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals left parenthesis StartRoot 7 EndRoot right parenthesis squared"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals 7"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. It follows that the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 a"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis"><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1b2b20b9","external_id":"a60b410d-c043-4ee9-8579-74c1c9e9aad2","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"8b017a0f-8fa9-4f7e-a95