<mi>s</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the slant height of the cone is <math alttext="85"><mn>85</mn>
</math> centimeters.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is one-third of the height, in centimeters, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the height, in centimeters, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the radius, in centimeters, of the base, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1be8b6b2","external_id":"aa19a0c6-76f9-4d66-b105-5e444ac3faec","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"a82b405f-882b-44c1-9407-a0443a36d322","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right circular cone has a volume of <math alttext=\"71,148 pi\"><mn>71,148</mn>\n<mi>&#960;</mi></math> cubic centimeters and the area of its base is <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&#960;</mi></math> square centimeters. What is the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"fe6f3306-46c9-4c0e-8e16-03e1195f00bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"14a28403-d777-4b12-a424-cccb9db95c45","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c6677c71-0a3c-4d30-8d5c-5c1e4eaf3488","content":"<p><math alttext=\"77\"><mn>77</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"67fc5222-0d00-4369-a487-25c140c69cf5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"85\"><mn>85</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["67fc5222-0d00-4369-a487-25c140c69cf5"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The volume, <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math>, of a right circular cone is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals one third pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mrow>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math> is the area of the circular base of the cone and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> is the height. It&rsquo;s given that this right circular cone has a volume of <math alttext=\"71,148 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>71,148</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> cubic centimeters and the area of its base is <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> square centimeters. Substituting <math alttext=\"71,148 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>71,148</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mrow>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals one third pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"71,148 pi equals left parenthesis one third right parenthesis left parenthesis 5,929 pi right parenthesis left parenthesis h right parenthesis\"><mn>71,148</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>5,929</mn><mi>&pi;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>h</mi></mfenced></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"12 equals StartFraction h Over 3 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mn>12</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>h</mi>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"36 equals h\"><mrow>\n<mn>36</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>h</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Let <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> represent the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone. A right triangle is formed by the radius, <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, height, <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math>, and slant height, <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>, of this cone, where <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> are the legs of the triangle and <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> is the hypotenuse. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the equation <math alttext=\"r squared plus h squared equals s squared\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> represents this relationship. Because <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is the area of the base and the area of the base is <math alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mrow>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>, it follows that <math alttext=\"5,929 pi equals pi r squared\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mi>&pi;</mi>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"pi\"><mi>&pi;</mi>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"5,929 equals r squared\"><mrow>\n<mn>5,929</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"5,929\"><mn>5,929</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"r squared\"><msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"r squared plus h squared equals s squared\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"5,929 plus 36 squared equals s squared\"><mn>5,929</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>36</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"5,929 plus 1,296 equals s squared\"><mn>5,929</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1,296</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"7,225 equals s squared\"><mrow>\n<mn>7,225</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>s</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"85 equals s\"><mrow>\n<mn>85</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>s</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the slant height of the cone is <math alttext=\"85\"><mn>85</mn>\n</math> centimeters.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is one-third of the height, in centimeters, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the height, in centimeters, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the radius, in centimeters, of the base, not the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554985,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"1be8b6b2","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1743430554985,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"aa19a0c6-76f9-4d66-b105-5e444ac3faec","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"a82b405f-882b-44c1-9407-a0443a36d322","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right circular cone has a volume of <math alttext=\"71,148 pi\"><mn>71,148</mn>\n<mi>&#960;</mi></math> cubic centimeters and the area of its base is <math alttext=\"5,929 pi\"><mn>5,929</mn>\n<mi>&#960;</mi></math> square centimeters. What is the slant height, in centimeters, of this cone?</p>","keys":["67fc5222-0d00-4369-a487-25c140c69cf5"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"fe6f3306-46c9-4c0e-8e16-03e1195f00bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"14a28403-d777-4b12-a424-cccb9db95c45","content":"<p><math altt