th xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E\"><mi>E</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"97 degree\"><mn>97</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It's also given that in triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"47 degree\"><mn>47</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the measure of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"97 degree\"><mn>97</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It follows that angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi></math> is congruent to angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi></math> and that angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E\"><mi>E</mi></math> is congruent to angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi></math>. Therefore, triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;is similar to triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;and no additional information is needed.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"c58fbfdc-93b3-4cba-83da-ffc2c85dd427","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017723,"updateDate":1755117017723}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017723, 1755117017723),
    ($SATQ$2266984b$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$08283-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><p class="standalone_statement style:1 "><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_004_7cd22920.png" alt="x squared, plus 20 x, plus y squared, plus 16 y, equals negative 20"></span></span></p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The equation above defines a circle in the <span class="italic"><span class="italic ">xy</span></span>-plane. What are the coordinates of the center of the circle?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_000_ab529003.png\" alt=\"negative 20 comma negative 16\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_001_425cefc1.png\" alt=\"negative 10 comma negative 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_002_9821eaec.png\" alt=\"10 comma 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_003_64b82dca.png\" alt=\"20 comma 16\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The standard equation of a circle in the <span class="italic">xy</span>-plane is of the form <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_005_b7cf5f79.png" alt="open parenthesis, x minus h, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y minus k, close parenthesis, squared, equals r squared"></span>, where <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_006_e0ba2fc4.png" alt="the ordered pair h comma k"></span>&nbsp;are the coordinates of the center of the circle and <span class="italic">r</span> is the radius. The given equation can be rewritten in standard form by completing the squares. So the sum of the first two terms, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_007_369087dc.png" alt="x squared, plus 20 x"></span>, needs a 100 to complete the square, and the sum of the second two terms, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_008_935177de.png" alt="y squared, plus 16 y"></span>, needs a 64 to complete the square. Adding 100 and 64 to both sides of the given equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_009_ce37f3e8.png" alt="open parenthesis, x squared, plus 20 x, plus 100, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, y squared, plus 16 y, plus 64, close parenthesis, equals negative 20, plus 100, plus 64"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_010_b2981df0.png" alt="open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y plus 8, close parenthesis, squared, equals 144"></span>. Therefore, the coordinates of the center of the circle are <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_011_fce59b83.png" alt="negative 10 comma negative 8"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from computational errors made when attempting to complete the squares or when identifying the coordinates of the center.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 12, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"2266984b","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"08283-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_004_7cd22920.png\" alt=\"x squared, plus 20 x, plus y squared, plus 16 y, equals negative 20\"></span></span></p></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The equation above defines a circle in the <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">xy</span></span>-plane. What are the coordinates of the center of the circle?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_000_ab529003.png\" alt=\"negative 20 comma negative 16\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_001_425cefc1.png\" alt=\"negative 10 comma negative 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_002_9821eaec.png\" alt=\"10 comma 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_003_64b82dca.png\" alt=\"20 comma 16\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The standard equation of a circle in the <span class=\"italic\">xy</span>-plane is of the form <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_005_b7cf5f79.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x minus h, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y minus k, close parenthesis, squared, equals r squared\"></span>, where <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_006_e0ba2fc4.png\" alt=\"the ordered pair h comma k\"></span>&nbsp;are the coordinates of the center of the circle and <span class=\"italic\">r</span> is the radius. The given equation can be rewritten in standard form by completing the squares. So the sum of the first two terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_007_369087dc.png\" alt=\"x squared, plus 20 x\"></span>, needs a 100 to complete the square, and the sum of the second two terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_008_935177de.png\" alt=\"y squared, plus 16 y\"></span>, needs a 64 to complete the square. Adding 100 and 64 to both sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_009_ce37f3e8.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x squared, plus 20 x, plus 100, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, y squared, plus 16 y, plus 64, close parenthesis, equals negative 20, plus 100, plus 64\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_010_b2981df0.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y plus 8, close parenthesis, squared, equals 144\"></span>. Therefore, the coordinates of the center of the circle are <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/2266984b/img_011_fce59b83.png\" alt=\"negative 10 comma negative 8\"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from computational errors made when attempting to complete the squares or when identifying the coordinates of the center.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":12,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959635,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"2266984b","skill_cd":"S.D.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Circles","createDate":1691007959635,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"08283-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"37cd15af-2ad4-43d3-938e-94b4d86613d5","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"08283-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, plus 20 x, plus y squared, plus 16 y, equals negative 20\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The equation above defines a circle in the <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">xy</span></span>-plane. What are the coordinates of the center of the circle?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 20 comma negative 16\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 10 comma negative 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"10 comma 8\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"20 comma 16\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The standard equation of a circle in the <span class=\"italic\">xy</span>-plane is of the form <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x minus h, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y minus k, close parenthesis, squared, equals r squared\"></span>, where <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the ordered pair h comma k\"></span>&nbsp;are the coordinates of the center of the circle and <span class=\"italic\">r</span> is the radius. The given equation can be rewritten in standard form by completing the squares. So the sum of the first two terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x squared, plus 20 x\"></span>, needs a 100 to complete the square, and the sum of the second two terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y squared, plus 16 y\"></span>, needs a 64 to complete the square. Adding 100 and 64 to both sides of the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x squared, plus 20 x, plus 100, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, y squared, plus 16 y, plus 64, close parenthesis, equals negative 20, plus 100, plus 64\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y plus 8, close parenthesis, squared, equals 144\"></span>. Therefore, the coordinates of the center of the circle are <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"negative 10 comma negative 8\"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from computational errors made when attempting to complete the squares or when identifying the coordinates of the center.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959635,"updateDate":1691007959635}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959635, 1691007959635),
